{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792589502,"nonce":"DrHNUz3ZLnSgd/+g5iC6AY/UkXo=","title":"TypeScript: reuse prelowered project HIR from shared snapshots","message":"The opt-in source-project cache restores checked AST but repeats native lowering, optimization and release analysis on each run. Extend the shared snapshot preparation/publication path to cache a linked project as split HIR, without another cache format or cloning frontend bodies to lower them twice. Keep check-only cache creation free of HIR work.\n\nValidate all source and resolution inputs (including type-only dependencies), compiler/frontend/policy compatibility, initializer ordering and once-only execution, exported generic templates, typed native GEPs and static releases. Cached programs must still enter through the interpreter and support Cranelift/LLVM promotion, with unused split bodies remaining encoded. Missing/corrupt/stale cache entries rebuild from checked source; unavailable persistence must not prevent execution. Compare cold, AST-hit and HIR-hit phase/allocation costs and report startup results without conflating eliminated and deferred work.\n\nParent: 0c26889a7cd2c4060eb94ef93fd808c2857089dbf714735ca52b5d071bdb1564.","files":null}]}